diagnosis_text:
The Kath4 lab is entirely healthy. A thorough investigation of every
component in the reported fault path found no defect.

Router16's two OSPF adjacencies (to mswitch0 at 10.2.2.2 via bond0, and to
router7 at 172.30.1.2 via eth2) are both in the Full/DR or Full/Backup state
and have been stable for over six minutes. Both of router16's active
interfaces (bond0 172.30.1.1/24 and eth2 10.2.2.1/24) are UP and carry no
iptables filtering rules; IP forwarding is enabled. Mswitch0 correctly holds
the three Campus 1 VLAN gateways (172.16.10.254, 172.16.20.254,
172.16.30.254) as connected routes on its vlan10/20/30 sub-interfaces, and
redistributes them into OSPF area 0. Every WAN router examined (router7,
router1, router11) carries OSPF-learned routes to all three 172.16.x.x/24
prefixes via the router7–router16 link. Data-plane probes confirm zero packet
loss in every direction tested: router7→pc5 (172.16.10.5), router11→all three
Campus 1 gateways, and pc5→router11 WAN address (10.1.1.1). The helpdesk
ticket describes a condition that does not exist in the live lab. The
operations staff member's recollection of a past router16 failure does not
reflect the current state. No corrective action is required; the reported
symptom is a false premise.
=== END ===
